data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded its dependency from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1.x to v2.x**, which targets OpenAPI v3.1. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

## Key Changes

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `JsonNode` (native System.Text.Json) |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | `schema.Type` includes `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiResponse { ... }` | Same, but `Responses` is now `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (no behavioral change here) |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` (moved namespace) |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` as `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Now has a `Schemes` dictionary property |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;           // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;  // for OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString → JsonNode
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // OpenApiSecurityScheme with Reference → OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");

    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable bool → Type flag composition
                // Remove "null" from the type set to make it non-nullable
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create(...)`** — all `IOpenApiAny` primitives are replaced by `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode`.
2. **`schema.Nullable = false`** → **`schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`** — OpenAPI 3.1 uses the JSON Schema `type` array instead of a `nullable` keyword.
3. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme` with `Reference`** → **`OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")`** — reference wrapper types replace manual `OpenApiReference` construction.
4. **`SecurityRequirement` indexer** → **`.Schemes` property** — the type no longer inherits from `Dictionary`; use the explicit property.
